    "title": "Where to watch Brazil vs. France live stream, TV channel, start time for international friendly",
    "text": "Where to watch Brazil vs. France live stream, TV channel, start time for international friendly originally appeared on The Sporting News. Add The Sporting News as a Preferred Source by clicking here.A highly-anticipated international friendly matchup between Brazil and France this week could be a preview into the 2026 FIFA World Cup.AdvertisementPart of the friendly series \"Road To 26\", these two iconic national teams will meet at Gillette Stadium in Boston on Thursday, marking their first head-to-head since 2015. The French side should familiarize themselves with Foxborough, as they'll be based there this summer during the tournament.Brazil enters this matchup on the heels of some defensive losses, with Arsenal's Gabriel Magalhaes, Liverpool's Alisson Becker and veteran left-back Alex Sandro all pulling out from the squad. While anything can happen, Carlo Ancelotti's side looks to be the underdog heading to Boston.Who can build momentum ahead of the World Cup?Here's everything you need to know about Brazil vs. France, including TV channel and streaming options for the international friendly match.AdvertisementHere's how to watch this international friendly match in the U.S.:TV channel: ESPN2Live stream: Fubo, ESPN appThis game will be broadcast on ESPN 2 and have streaming options available on Fubo and the ESPN app.Fubo offers a free trial for new subscribers, so you can try the service before you buy. Stream ESPN, ABC, CBS, Fox and 100+ top channels of live TV and sports without cable. (Participating plans only. Taxes and fees may apply.)Now you can watch ESPN without cable. Stream live NBA, NFL, MLB, NHL, college sports, plus SportsCenter, First Take, and all your favorite ESPN shows—anytime, anywhere—only in the ESPN app.AdvertisementWhat time does France vs. Brazilkick off?This international friendly matchup takes place at Gillette Stadium in Foxborough, Massachusetts and kicks off on Thursday, March 26 at 4 p.m. local time.Here's how that time translates across the U.S.:DateKickoff timeEastern TimeThu, Mar. 264 p.m.Central TimeThu, Mar. 263 p.m.Mountain TimeThu, Mar. 262 p.m.Pacific TimeThu, Mar. 261 p.m.International friendly fixture schedule todayThursday, March 26Aruba vs. Macau (7:30 a.m. ET)Vietnam vs. Bangladesh (8 a.m. ET)Tanzania vs. Liechtenstein (10:30 a.m. ET)Moldova vs. Lithuania (11 a.m. ET)Cyprus vs. Belarus (1 p.m. ET)Georgia vs. Israel (1 p.m. ET)Brazil vs. France (4 p.m. ET)Martinique vs. Cuba (5 p.m. ET)Bahamas vs. Anguilla (5:30 p.m. ET)St. Martin vs. Barbados (6 p.m. ET)Colombia vs. Croatia (7:30 p.m. ET)Cayman Islands vs. British Virgin Islands (8 p.m. ET)Dominican Republic vs. El Salvador (8 p.m. ET)Bonaire vs. St. Vincent and the Grenadines (8:30 p.m. ET)Chile vs. Cape Verde (11 p.m. ET)",
